# Copy to `.env` and adjust. Optional: copy secrets to `.env.local` so they stay out of the
# encrypted base file (see below).
#
# --- dotenvx ---
# This app loads env with `@dotenvx/dotenvx` (see `src/load-env.ts`).
#
# • Local dev (default): reads `apps/api/.env` then `apps/api/.env.local` (optional overrides).
# • Production DB commands from your machine: use the `*:prod` scripts or set
#   `PULSE_ENV_FILE_TARGET=production` so only `apps/api/.env.production` is loaded
#   (see `package.json` `db:*:prod` scripts). That file is not layered on `.env` — it must
#   contain every variable those commands need. Missing `DATABASE_URL` fails fast
#   (`src/validate-env.ts`).
#
# • Running the API with NODE_ENV=production (e.g. `pnpm start`): `DATABASE_URL` and
#   `CORS_ORIGIN` are required (same validation module).
#
# Encrypt files so the team shares one `.env.keys` per environment instead of copying full
# `.env` blobs between machines (keys stay out of git):
#
#   pnpm exec dotenvx encrypt -f .env
#   pnpm exec dotenvx encrypt -f .env.production
#
# Keep `apps/api/.env.keys` locally or in your password manager — it is gitignored.
# Encrypted `.env` files may be committed once your team agrees on that workflow.
#
# --- API ---
PORT=4000
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
LOG_LEVEL=debug

# Clerk
CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=

ADMIN_API_KEY=

NATSTAT_BASE_URL=https://api4.natst.at
NATSTAT_API_KEY=

# Database (local Docker / Postgres)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://pulse:pulse_dev_password@localhost:5432/pulse_dev

# --- `.env.production` (isolated; copy from here and fill for Supabase / hosted API) ---
# Required for `db:*:prod` scripts: DATABASE_URL
# Required when serving with NODE_ENV=production: DATABASE_URL, CORS_ORIGIN
# Strongly recommended: CLERK_*, ADMIN_API_KEY, NATSTAT_*, PORT, LOG_LEVEL
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@db.<project>.supabase.co:5432/postgres
# CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-app.example.com
